{"source_id": "W2510835855", "title": "Comparing note taking and test performance in methods and modes of note taking conditions", "year": 2016, "abstract": "Note taking is a common and effective practice among college students to support learning during lectures. Generally, there are two justifications for perceived benefits from note taking: the encoding function and the external storage function. The encoding function posits that the process of taking notes facilitates learning, whereas the external storage function posits that notes serve as a record to be reviewed later. The present study compared longhand and laptop note taking and examined test performance under conditions where notes were or were not reviewed. Results indicated that longhand note takers outperformed laptop note takers on factual recall, but this advantage disappeared when participants reviewed their notes."}
